    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\ncompletion\n\n### Description\n\nI think it would be good to have an option, for the completion UI to only show with after a minimum number of characters in a word. I currently run into this with numbers a lot. Those almost always trigger the completion popup, are rarely usefull and capture the arrow keys. This makes changing a bunch of numbers pretty tedious.\r\n\r\nIn general i think i rarely want to complete from a single letter. So, having a config option to only show the popup after 2 or 3 characters would be great.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, a character deny list might be an idea. That way one could exclude numbers from completion.",
