    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThe main reason for not implementing \"minimum number of character to trigger completion\" type of functionality is that it would significantly increase computational load (by computing completion word on every typed character). Right now only the inserted key is checked for being a part of a \"keyword\" and is basically free because it comes with `InsertCharPre` event.\r\n\r\nThe suggested way of tackling this is by increasing `delay.completion` so that it won't trigger after single character (albeit affecting all autocompletion).\r\n\r\nHaving a \"blocklist\" type of functionality is doable but also comes with a computational cost, as that list must be constructed from global and buffer-local config on every  character type to allow users set it interactively.\r\n\r\nSo I am not keen on adding this kind of functionality, but I'll think about it a bit more.",
