        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "With up and down arrow, you can highlight one of the completion options. I'd like to remap that to <C-H/J>.\r\n\r\nOne usecase that comes up quite often for me, are lists of IP adresses. I get maybe a list of 10 or 15 IP adresses where i need to change the last number to something else. Nothing with a pattern, just manual changes. I go into insert mode, and just backspace, replace, down etc.\r\nIt help that my keyboard has the arrow keys mapped to hjkl on a layer, but that's besides the point. I can't really write a macro for that as there's no pattern, but every number triggers the popup, requiring and extra keypress to dismiss it, and also putting me back to normal mode, which makes my workflow more or less not doable.\r\n\r\nMaybe there's a better \"vim-way\" of doing what i do, but going into insert mode and back to normal mode for one-character edits on multiple lines feels repetitive, when i can just do it all in Insert mode.\r\n",
