        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> With up and down arrow, you can highlight one of the completion options. I'd like to remap that to <C-H/J>.\r\n\r\nThose actions come from Neovim's built-in way of handling completion and can be modified with custom mappings.\r\n\r\nThat can also be done with `<C-n>` / `<C-p>` (as in \"next\" / \"previous\") and is arguable a more \"vim way\". If you don't like them, you can slightly modify the [example in the docs about `<Tab>` / `<S-Tab>`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f699158e6a654d2778e446d98de2881d7ab1f5fb/doc/mini-completion.txt#L101-L104).",
